'''Calabazas''' ({{IPA-bl|kə.ɾəˈβa.sə}}; {{Langx|kp|Kõay Pytã|4=red {{W|gourd}}}}), is the [[w:Capital city|administrative seat]] and most populous city within the [[Araucaria]]n region of [[Brasal]]. It is considered to be the southern extremity of the [[Concordia]] conurbation, and is the [[List of cities in Balisca by population|21st largest city in Balisca by population]].

The city's name refers to the "{{W|Calabash|calabash}}", translated as ''calabaza'' ("pumpkin; orange colour"), which were cultivated by early settlers. Major settlement in the area began following the eruption of the [[Maroon Wars]] the early 17th century. At the turn of the 20th century, the city had a reputation as one of the most dangerous port cities in the archipelago and a hub for [[Baliscan Mafia|organized crime]], such as [[W:Prostitution|prostitution]], [[W:Racketeering|racketeering]] and smuggling. During Balisca's shift to a [[W:War economy|war economy]] amid the [[Great Adonian War]], Calabazas experienced an economic revitalization as a major port of embarkment for troops destined to the [[Balboa Campaign]], and its hard-edged reputation rapidly dissipated.

Today the local economy predominately consists of small and medium-sized {{W|cooperative}}s in the service sector, with an emphasis on [[W:Social care|social care]], business services, and tourism. The city is a major tourist destination with a sunny, {{W|oceanic climate}} and has become widely known for its world-class trails, picturesque cliffs, theme parks, nightlife. 

It is one of the more prominent center of Balisca's [[Entertainment industry in Balisca|film and special effects industries]], and increasingly a hub for information technology and innovation, hosting the headquarters of Baliscan tech giant [[Aletech]]. Together with neighboring [[Jatiel]], the city is served by [[Alunzaro International Airport|Alunzaro Airport]], the fourth busiest airport in the country.  

